{\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn\b Planted defects (appendix I.4)\par}
{\pard\sa160 {\f1 mark1 inject <paper>} makes one copy of a record per defect in {\f1 defected/<paper>--<defect>/}, each with a {\f1 defect.yaml} stating the findings it should produce. {\f1 mark1 evaluate <paper>} checks every copy and writes {\f1 defects-<paper>.md}. The copies are restamped as if the author's generator had produced their AI appendix from the defected paper, so each defect is caught by the check it targets rather than by a stale stamp.\par}
